<title>SPAIN: Spain's Fenosa parent pretax profit up 13.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain's Fenosa parent pretax profit up 13.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for Spanish utility Union Fenosa for year to 1996 in billions of pesetas, unless stated:</p>
<p> Pretax profit			    23.57   up   13.7 pct</p>
<p> Cash flow				  77.06   up   10.4 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures refer to parent company alone, a spokesman for Fenosa said.  </p>
<p>In a statement, Fenosa said operating costs were flat in 1996, while personnel costs fell 1.3 percent.</p>
<p>Financial charges fell 16.4 percent.</p>
<p>Investment in plant was over 31.5 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>Debt stood at 477.29 billion pesetas at year-end, having fallen by 27.23 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>The spokesman said no net profit figures for the group were available.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
